<title>NORWAY: Statoil starts Nor-Fra pipe work in France.</title>
<headline>Statoil starts Nor-Fra pipe work in France.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Work to pull the NorFra gas trunkline ashore began at Dunkerque in northern France this week, about a fortnight ahead of schedule, Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil ) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said roughly 160 km had so far been laid of the 840 km which will make this facility the world's longest submarine pipeline.</p>
<p>A jack-up rig, three dredgers and three barges have prepared the pipeline route across the beach at Dunkerque in a 500-metre trench walled with sheet piles.</p>
<p>The whole line is due to be completed in October, with gas deliveries starting a year later, Status Weekly said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
